{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.GCTSchurMultiplicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.GCTSchurMultiplicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.GCTMultiplicityObstruction","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.schur_separatedAt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.schur_separatedAt_two","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTSchurMultiplicity.lean#L121-L126","doc":"**Concrete GCT obstruction (sorry-free).**  At `N = 1` the block `[2]` is\npresent at the substrate and dropped at the TL locus `X = Q^{-1}` — an\nexplicit, proved multiplicity drop separating the two regimes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hasContentCell_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hasContentCell_two","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTSchurMultiplicity.lean#L116-L119","doc":"**Concrete non-vacuity: `[2]` has a content-`1` cell.**  The cell `(0,1)` of\nthe partition `[2]` has content `1 − 0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.schur_multData_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.schur_multData_ne","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTSchurMultiplicity.lean#L109-L114","doc":"The two multiplicity data genuinely differ (via `multData_ne_of_separatedAt`):\nthe substrate and TL-locus Wedderburn decompositions are distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.schur_separatedAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.schur_separatedAt","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTSchurMultiplicity.lean#L93-L107","doc":"**A proved OCCURRENCE separation (sorry-free).**  The substrate data\n`schurMult Q (-1)` (all blocks present) and the TL-locus data\n`schurMult Q (Q^{-N})` (content-`N` blocks dropped) are `SeparatedAt` every\ncontent-`N` partition: `1 ≠ 0`.\n\n**Not a multiplicity obstruction.**  `schurMult` is a 0/1 presence\nindicator, so this separates by occurrence, and Bürgisser–Ikenmeyer–Panova\nprove occurrence obstructions cannot separate `VP` from `VNP`.  See the\nmodule docstring's correction record before citing this as GCT progress. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.schurMult_tl_drop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.schurMult_tl_drop","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTSchurMultiplicity.lean#L85-L91","doc":"**TL locus: a content-`N` block is dropped (sorry-free).**  At `X = Q^{-N}` a\npartition with a content-`N` cell has vanishing Schur element, so its\nmultiplicity drops to `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.schurMult_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.schurMult_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTSchurMultiplicity.lean#L78-L83","doc":"**Substrate: every block present (sorry-free).**  For `Q > 1`, `X ≤ 0` no\nSchur element vanishes, so every multiplicity is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.schurMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.schurMult","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTSchurMultiplicity.lean#L72-L76","doc":"**GCT multiplicity indicator.**  `1` if the Wedderburn block `λ` is present\n(Schur element nonzero), `0` if dropped (Schur element zero) — the block's\nmultiplicity in the (semisimple or TL-truncated) decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}